WEBVTT

00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:10.033
Aah!

00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:11.382
Hmm?

00:00:17.954 --> 00:00:18.868
[SIGHS]

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.873
MAVIS: Johnny! Come quick!

00:00:24.047 --> 00:00:24.961
[PANTING]

00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:28.486
What's up? He's okay?

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.923
Dennis said
his first word! [CHUCKLING]

00:00:30.445 --> 00:00:31.751
He did?

00:00:31.925 --> 00:00:33.796
Come on, honey.
Say it again.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:34.928
Bleh, bleh-bleh.

00:00:36.364 --> 00:00:38.845
I don't say,
"Bleh, bleh-bleh."

00:00:39.802 --> 00:00:41.543
We didn't say you did.

00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:42.587
Then where did
he get that?

00:00:42.762 --> 00:00:43.980
Bleh, bleh-bleh.

00:00:44.154 --> 00:00:46.330
Well,
maybe sometimes you say it.

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:48.463
I only say it when I
say I don't say it!

00:00:48.985 --> 00:00:50.378
Bleh, bleh-bleh.

00:00:50.552 --> 00:00:52.946
Okay, kid.
We get it. You can talk.

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:56.210
Denisovich.

00:00:57.515 --> 00:00:58.821
MAVIS: Dad.

00:00:58.995 --> 00:00:59.996
Just checking for cavities.

00:01:03.521 --> 00:01:04.740
Bleh, bleh-bleh.

00:01:04.914 --> 00:01:06.046
Bleh, bleh-bleh.

00:01:06.742 --> 00:01:08.178
It was you!

00:01:08.788 --> 00:01:09.571
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:14.054 --> 00:01:15.055
[PHONE RINGING]

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:16.056
[MR. BIGFOOT LAUGHING]

00:01:19.276 --> 00:01:20.495
HUMAN FLY:
Oh, my goodness, Leonard.

00:01:20.669 --> 00:01:22.236
If you really
looked that hideous,

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.064
I don't think I
could hang out with you.

00:01:24.238 --> 00:01:25.674
[CHUCKLING] Guys, what's the deal?

00:01:25.848 --> 00:01:28.677
Is this a party?
Pick up a phone.

00:01:28.851 --> 00:01:33.943
I don't care if Johnny
said it's a "cool app."
Johnny's still new here.

00:01:34.117 --> 00:01:37.294
Now, Porridge Head,
did you call a hearse
for the Gremlinbergs?

00:01:37.468 --> 00:01:40.776
No, you're checking
your Facebook page. Again.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.604
Drac,
I told the guys social media

00:01:42.778 --> 00:01:44.084
is the best way to
promote the hotel.

00:01:44.258 --> 00:01:45.433
Right, Clifton?[GROANS]

00:01:47.478 --> 00:01:49.567
So, Drac, I wanted
to go through
some thoughts I had,

00:01:49.741 --> 00:01:52.614
as your new human relations
coordinating co-assistant.

00:01:52.788 --> 00:01:54.921
Sure. It's a real job.

00:01:55.095 --> 00:01:57.097
Not a cheap excuse
to keep Mavis happy,
so you never leave here.

00:01:57.271 --> 00:01:59.795
Right. So,
I was thinking,

00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:03.755
since we have so
many humans now,
maybe update some of the acts?

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.235
Like, maybe the magician?

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:07.324
What's wrong with
Harry Three-Eye?

00:02:07.498 --> 00:02:10.501
Well, he might be
a little old-school
for the humans.

00:02:10.675 --> 00:02:12.590
Tell me,
sir, what was your card?

00:02:12.764 --> 00:02:14.157
The three of spades?

00:02:16.159 --> 00:02:18.335
Is this your card, my friend?

00:02:19.119 --> 00:02:20.207
Whoa!

00:02:20.381 --> 00:02:21.121
[ALL EXCLAIMING]

00:02:22.296 --> 00:02:24.080
No, Harry's great.

00:02:24.254 --> 00:02:26.169
Can't blame Harry
for the crowd
not being hip.

00:02:26.343 --> 00:02:28.389
Okay, what about Wayne?

00:02:28.563 --> 00:02:30.043
Wayne?
Are you nuts?
He's my boy.

00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:31.958
Then maybe something
other than tennis?

00:02:32.132 --> 00:02:34.221
Okay, so, what you wanna do

00:02:34.395 --> 00:02:37.702
is lift the racket
right on impact, so
you get that nice top spin.

00:02:37.877 --> 00:02:39.313
Try and hit one.

00:02:40.575 --> 00:02:41.271
[BARKING]

00:02:46.624 --> 00:02:48.888
[PANTING]

00:02:49.062 --> 00:02:51.064
[CELL PHONE VIBRATING] What is that?
What's the noise? It's on me!

00:02:51.238 --> 00:02:53.370
It's just
the cell phone I got you.

00:02:53.544 --> 00:02:56.069
Clifton's sending you a text
so you can practice
how to write back.

00:02:56.243 --> 00:02:57.374
[CELL PHONE CHIMES] Oh!

00:02:58.854 --> 00:03:00.029
Eh...

00:03:00.203 --> 00:03:01.291
What the...
It's not doing it.

00:03:01.465 --> 00:03:02.466
I got it.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.207
[JONATHAN READING]

00:03:07.994 --> 00:03:09.082
Now you can text Clifton.

00:03:10.126 --> 00:03:11.388
All right, fine.

00:03:12.694 --> 00:03:14.130
How do you do this?

00:03:14.304 --> 00:03:15.523
JONATHAN:
Maybe it's your fingernails.

00:03:15.697 --> 00:03:17.699
It's easy.
Look. I'll text Mavis.

00:03:17.873 --> 00:03:20.745
Psyched for date night.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.052
[CELL PHONE CHIMES]See? And now look,
she texted right back.

00:03:23.226 --> 00:03:25.272
"Gotta cancel.
Can't leave Dennis."

00:03:25.881 --> 00:03:27.274
Okay.

00:03:27.448 --> 00:03:31.843
Are we never
allowed to be alone again?

00:03:32.018 --> 00:03:35.717
I need to feel loved, too.

00:03:35.891 --> 00:03:38.589
And send.

00:03:38.763 --> 00:03:41.897
Okay. All that taught me
is that you're pathetic.

00:03:42.071 --> 00:03:44.204
Yeah, got it.
Maybe you should
just get Bluetooth.

00:03:44.378 --> 00:03:46.641
Okay.
Blue Tooth, come over here.

00:03:49.687 --> 00:03:50.993
So, now what?

00:03:55.519 --> 00:03:57.695
Rise and shine, my Denisovich.

00:03:57.869 --> 00:03:59.610
Hi, Papa.

00:03:59.784 --> 00:04:02.918
Hello, my little devil.
Did you have sweet nightmares?

00:04:03.092 --> 00:04:06.748
Uh-huh. I dreamed
that I saw a stegosaurus.

00:04:06.922 --> 00:04:09.055
Oh... And were you
drinking his blood?

00:04:09.707 --> 00:04:10.926
No.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.406
Just throwing it out there.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:13.798
Hey! You want to
do something cool?

00:04:13.973 --> 00:04:16.497
Yeah! [CHUCKLES]

00:04:16.671 --> 00:04:21.067
I'm going to teach you
how to turn into a bat.
Like me.

00:04:21.241 --> 00:04:22.938
See? [CHUCKLES] Cool.

00:04:23.112 --> 00:04:24.766
Yes! Cool, like I said.

00:04:25.593 --> 00:04:26.724
Now you try.

00:04:27.638 --> 00:04:29.162
I'm a bat. [GIGGLES]

00:04:29.336 --> 00:04:31.077
I'm a bat.
I'm a bat. I'm a bat.

00:04:31.251 --> 00:04:32.295
I'm a bat.

00:04:33.122 --> 00:04:34.558
I mean, a real bat.

00:04:34.732 --> 00:04:36.125
I'm a bat!

00:04:36.299 --> 00:04:38.301
[BLOWS A RASPBERRY]

00:04:38.475 --> 00:04:42.610
Denisovich. Take a breath.
You can really
turn into a bat.

00:04:42.784 --> 00:04:44.786
Try. Feel the bat.

00:04:47.136 --> 00:04:48.616
Not a chicken.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.099
What's that?
The electric boogaloo?

00:04:53.273 --> 00:04:55.971
If I show you I
can bust a move,
will you try to fly, then?

00:04:56.145 --> 00:04:57.016
Uh-huh.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.104
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:05:12.074 --> 00:05:13.815
Dad? Why are you guys dancing?

00:05:15.034 --> 00:05:17.166
Uh, he was sleep-dancing.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.776
Come on, sweetie.
Back to bed.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:21.562
"Back to bed"?
It's already after 8:00 p.m.

00:05:21.736 --> 00:05:23.564
Don't you remember
the new sleep schedule?

00:05:23.738 --> 00:05:24.478
He's going to human
classes half the day.

00:05:24.652 --> 00:05:27.046
Uh...

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.439
If he could just sleep
till 2:00 a.m. tonight,
it'd be so great for him.

00:05:29.613 --> 00:05:31.441
But, honeydeath,
six of Wayne's wolf pups

00:05:31.615 --> 00:05:33.443
are having
a birthday party tonight.

00:05:33.617 --> 00:05:35.837
You wouldn't want
him to miss that.

00:05:36.011 --> 00:05:39.449
Dad, I love the wolf pups,
but they're a little
too rough for Dennis.

00:05:39.623 --> 00:05:41.756
"Too rough"?

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:43.975
Haven't you noticed?
Dennis is different.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.674
What are you saying?
Denisovich shouldn't
be around monsters?

00:05:46.848 --> 00:05:50.025
I love monsters!
Video! Video! Ha!

00:05:50.199 --> 00:05:52.158
Oh, you wanna show Papa Drac
your monster video?

00:05:52.332 --> 00:05:53.246
Yeah! [CHUCKLES]

00:05:56.205 --> 00:05:58.207
MAN ON TV:
Who's the coolest monster?

00:05:58.381 --> 00:06:00.079
ALL: Kakie!

00:06:00.253 --> 00:06:03.082
Wee! Kakie one happy monster!

00:06:03.256 --> 00:06:05.693
Kakie love cake! Yummy!

00:06:05.867 --> 00:06:08.130
Tummy get a tummyache.

00:06:08.304 --> 00:06:11.525
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
How is that a monster?

00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:13.701
KAKIE: Have some cake,
Wuzzlelumplebum.

00:06:13.875 --> 00:06:17.748
Remember, kids,
a real monster always shares.

00:06:17.922 --> 00:06:22.579
"Shares"? Yes!
When I think monsters,
I think "shares."

00:06:22.753 --> 00:06:26.148
Now, let me tell you
what a real
monster is, Denisovich.

00:06:26.322 --> 00:06:29.891
Dad, please. He's
practically five already.
Don't force it.

00:06:33.764 --> 00:06:35.853
Slow down, Wuzzlelumplebum.

00:06:36.027 --> 00:06:39.509
[LAUGHING]

00:06:41.511 --> 00:06:44.949
♪ Twinkle,
twinkle, little star
How I wonder ♪

00:06:45.124 --> 00:06:47.474
Mommy,
I'm too old for lullabies.

00:06:47.648 --> 00:06:49.737
What?
That's not how that one goes.

00:06:49.911 --> 00:06:51.391
This is the way
most people sing it.

00:06:51.565 --> 00:06:53.610
"Most people"?
What's wrong with...

00:06:53.784 --> 00:06:57.136
♪ Suffer, suffer,
scream in pain

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.617
♪ Blood is spilling
from your brain ♪

00:07:00.791 --> 00:07:03.359
Daddy. Come on. You know
how I sang it to you.

00:07:03.533 --> 00:07:06.536
♪ Zombies gnaw you
like a plum

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.800
♪ Piercing cries
and you succumb

00:07:11.498 --> 00:07:15.284
♪ Suffer, suffer,
scream in pain

00:07:15.458 --> 00:07:20.420
♪ You will never
breathe again ♪

00:07:22.683 --> 00:07:23.945
Still works.

00:07:31.126 --> 00:07:31.909
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:07:37.959 --> 00:07:38.612
[CHILDREN CHUCKLING]

00:07:44.183 --> 00:07:45.140
Oh...

00:07:45.314 --> 00:07:47.011
[GASPS]

00:07:47.186 --> 00:07:49.144
DENNIS: Happy birthday,
Wally, Wilson,

00:07:49.318 --> 00:07:51.146
Whoopi,
Waylon, Weepy and Wanye.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.104
[SQUEAKING]

00:07:53.279 --> 00:07:55.542
Denisovich!
My big boy! You made it! [LAUGHS]

00:07:56.586 --> 00:07:58.719
I thought about
what you said, Dad.

00:07:58.893 --> 00:08:00.503
Maybe I was being
a little overprotective.

00:08:00.677 --> 00:08:02.549
Thank you, coffin cake.

00:08:03.637 --> 00:08:05.116
Dennis! I love you! Zing!

00:08:05.291 --> 00:08:06.814
Hi, Winnie.

00:08:06.988 --> 00:08:09.991
I just love your
yummy strawberry locks!
Zing, zing!

00:08:13.212 --> 00:08:16.998
Winnie.
Give him his space, hon.
I'm sorry, Mavis.

00:08:17.172 --> 00:08:19.740
It's okay, Aunt Wanda.
They're just playing.

00:08:19.914 --> 00:08:23.483
Holy rabies! Limbo?
I used to love that game!

00:08:23.657 --> 00:08:25.354
Get in there, Mavey.

00:08:25.528 --> 00:08:27.008
Really? But I'm a parent now.

00:08:27.182 --> 00:08:28.488
Show 'em how it's done.

00:08:28.662 --> 00:08:29.837
Okay. Okay, okay.

00:08:33.188 --> 00:08:33.971
[ALL CHEERING]

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:36.887
[GASPS]

00:08:38.889 --> 00:08:40.456
No way! A pinata?

00:08:44.373 --> 00:08:45.983
Oh, Mavis, honey.
That's for later.

00:08:46.157 --> 00:08:47.985
MAVIS: Whoo! [CHUCKLES]

00:08:48.159 --> 00:08:49.030
We don't want
the pups to have too much...

00:08:50.249 --> 00:08:51.641
[ALL CHEERING] PUP: Candy!

00:08:55.254 --> 00:08:56.037
Sugar.

00:09:04.001 --> 00:09:05.960
I'm sorry.
Did I start all that?

00:09:06.134 --> 00:09:07.788
Don't worry.
There's a reason
they call it a litter.

